        <mxCell id="pjv6TpUX4W-IxdOAIxX1-402" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Crawling / Spider Subsystem&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;These are the tables necessary to administer the application reaching out to the web for additional information.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;We are hanging on to information in the early days, as this will be a prime dataset for regression testing and improving the prompts (via skills definition). Eventually, we won&#39;t hang on to zip files of everything that we download, as the space required will be excessive.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="250" x="1150" y="430" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pjv6TpUX4W-IxdOAIxX1-403" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=default;strokeColor=default;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Alternative Element Model&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this approach, all details of an entity are suspect. The entity is created. And it&#39;s details are recorded multiple times as information is gathered. I can see a maintenance routing that scans informations, bias towards recency, and maintains the the &quot;current&quot; details as the belief of the system.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="310" x="-770" y="-1240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
